  "title": "Problems with credentials for HTTP Request on self hosted N8N · Chase AI Community",
  "text": "1\nCommunity\nClassroom\nCalendar\nMembers\nMap\nLeaderboards\nAbout\nChase AI Community\n1\n1\nJonas Hermann\n12d • ⚡General discussion\nProblems with credentials for HTTP Request on self hosted N8N\nIm trying to do a firecrawl request via http Node in self hosted n8n (hostinger) and im running into an issue. Whenever I setup the credential and reload the page or actually test the flow it unplugs that credential again saying I have no credentials set up. When I setup a new credential suddenly the others that I setup are available. Whats going on here anyone can help?\nLike\n1\n2 comments\n2\nScott Jessen\n• 7d\n@Jonas Hermann It sounds like your encryption key isn't holding between restarts. I would check that `N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY` is set as a static env variable in your config, if it's not set, n8n generates a random one each boot and can't decrypt the credentials it saved previously.\n3\nReply\n1\nJonas Hermann\n• 5d\nThanks for the help that was exactly the fix that it needed\n1\nReply\n1\n\n\n\n\n1\nProblems with credentials for HTTP Request on self hosted N8N\nChase AI Community\nskool.com/chase-ai-community\nGo from learning to earning. Join Chase AI+👇\nUpgrade to Chase AI+\n57.5k\nMembers\n248\nOnline\n3\nAdmins\nINVITE PEOPLE\nLeaderboard (30-day)\n1\nVitalii Hryhorenko\n+51\n2\nCharles Dove\n🔥\n+23\n3\nCyber Ai\n+22\n4\nSam Alder\n🔥\n+16\n5\nJonathan Wilson\n+15\nSee all leaderboards\nPowered by",
